  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto recently hosted ten former Indonesian National Police chiefs to discuss ongoing security concerns, specifically the current investigation into the alleged illegal wiretapping of the president. This development occurs as various government stakeholders and political parties, including Gerindra and Golkar, demand an expansive and comprehensive inquiry into the potential breach. Legal expert Jimly Asshiddiqie has publicly stated that the incident potentially constitutes a case of treason, prompting calls for swift legal action. Simultaneously, law enforcement authorities have initiated formal procedures to secure the safety of six key witnesses through the Witness and Victim Protection Agency. While some officials have warned against political actors attempting to exploit the situation or implicate specific government members, the national focus remains on the progress of the police investigation to identify those responsible for the reported surveillance of the head of state.",
